<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Map</h1>
<p>There is no map command, but there are two kinds of map. The web client draws a map for you. When you 
walk somewhere that has a map, the map panel shows it with a mark where 
you stand, and the mark follows you as you walk. Click the map to see it 
large.
</p><p>Maps exist so far for Midgaard, Udgaard, the Haon-Dor and Cypress 
forests, and the guilds of the healers, fighters, conjurers and thieves. 
Elsewhere the panel waits: "The map appears when you walk somewhere that 
has one."
</p><p>Many areas also tell you about themselves: type <a cmd='#'>help area</a> to learn 
where you are and something about the place. In Midgaard, Udgaard, the 
barbarians' lands, the gremlins' and the guilds of the healers, fighters, 
conjurers and thieves, that includes a map drawn in letters, which works 
in any client.
</p><p>Everywhere, the compass beside the room name lights up the ways out (see 
<a cmd='#'>Help Exits</a>).
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Exits</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Movement</a>
</pre>




</div>